// The **Markdown** screen's two panes, under the header `MarkdownChapter` puts
// over them. Two nodes in it matter.
//
// `text-area` writes `md.source` through an action; `markdown-view` reads the
// same property with `bind=`. Nothing watches the editor, diffs the text or
// schedules a re-render: the element holding the preview is subscribed to the
// property, a keystroke marks it for rebuild, and the next frame is the parsed
// document. A live preview is a binding.
//
// `markdown-view` is also not this application's widget and this document never
// says where it comes from. `goldberry-html` is on the module path, its catalog
// declares the node name, and the inflater finds it.
//
// A `split-pane` at the root rather than a masonry: this screen is one thing
// divided, not a wall of cards, and it fills a tab that is not scrolled -- the
// preview owns a viewport, and scrollers on the same axis do not nest.
split-pane id="markdown-split" position=0.5 first-min=240 second-min=240 {
    column id="markdown-editor" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Markdown — type here"
        // `fill=#true` is the editor half of a `text-area`: the height comes
        // from this pane rather than from the text, and the document scrolls
        // inside it.
        text-area id="markdown-source" class="mono" bind="md.source" change="md.set-source" fill=#true
    }
    column id="markdown-preview" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Rendered — this side follows"
        // What the last pressed link or ticked box reported. `link=` and
        // `wikilink=` name valued actions that are handed a destination, and
        // `task=` is handed the ordinal of the box, which `Markdown.toggleTask`
        // turns into one changed character of the source on the left.
        text id="markdown-followed" class="caption" bind="md.followed"
        scroll {
            markdown-view id="markdown-rendered" bind="md.source" \
                link="md.follow" wikilink="md.open-wiki" task="md.toggle-task" images="app.assets"
        }
    }
}
